  "idea": "Simple keyboard shortcuts that save 100 hours of mouse clicking a year",
  "text": "Five essential keyboard shortcuts separate computer beginners from true power users every single day. Grabbing your mouse for basic edits repeatedly disrupts your concentration and slows your typing cadence. Reaching back and forth creates friction that quietly wastes thirty productive minutes each afternoon. Master Control-Z to undo errors, Control-F to search documents, and Windows-V to access clipboard history. You will work significantly faster without touching your trackpad.",
